INFO httpx: HTTP Request: POST https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic/v1/messages "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
    ✗ rebutted
      reason: The finding assumes that an attacker can control the `argv` 
parameter of the `main` function. However, `main` is a command-line entry point 
(e.g., `python -m aiohttp.web module:app`). The `argv` is supplied by the system
administrator or user who starts the server, not by an external network 
attacker. There is no evidence that this function is exposed to untrusted input 
over the network or that an attacker can influence `argv` without already having
code execution. Therefore, the described RCE scenario is not realistically 
exploitable in the intended use of the library. The code performs the intended 
dynamic import based on user-supplied arguments, which is a legitimate feature. 
No access control bypass or external injection vector is present.
