INFO httpx: HTTP Request: POST https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic/v1/messages "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
    ✗ rebutted
      reason: The finding is based on a body-only detection of a dangerous API 
(`pathlib.Path.open`) inside the `save` method. The source header explicitly 
marks `[REACHABILITY: BODY_ONLY]`, meaning no internal call chain was found that
passes attacker-controlled input to this function. The `save` method is a 
library utility in `aiohttp` intended for internal persistence of cookie jar 
data; it does not inherently accept untrusted input from external users. The 
library does not expose this method to remote attackers without explicit 
application-level misuse. Exploitation would require an application developer to
take user-supplied data and pass it directly to `save` — a scenario that is not 
part of the library's own code and is not demonstrated. Therefore, the 
vulnerability is not exploitable in the library's context and the finding must 
be rebutted.
